ib/ISLR2_1.3-2.tar.gz") ("source-version" . "ISLR2 1.3-2") ("source-sha256" . "d66f93907dea9417e21bd5252c8d862497762ecb44cd877dfc34665d162d5f52") ("sha256" . "9901c54893cca931d9255a1f17c18b775cb2a340d5bd5992eda0bff7e3dc70d9") ("license" . "GPL-2.0-only") ("citation" . "James, G., Witten, D., Hastie, T. and Tibshirani, R. (2022). ISLR2: Introduction to Statistical Learning, Second Edition. R package version 1.3-2. Book: An Introduction to Statistical Learning with Applications in R, Second Edition (2021), Springer, https://www.statlearning.com. Original sources in the bundled upstream documentation.") ("notes" . "The data contains 5822 real customer records. Each record consists of 86 variables, containing sociodemographic data (variables 1-43) and product ownership (variables 44-86). The sociodemographic data is derived from zip codes. All customers living in areas with the same zip code have the same sociodemographic attributes. Variable 86 (Purchase) indicates whether the customer purchased a caravan insurance policy. Further information on the individual variables can be obtained at http://www.liacs.nl/~putten/library/cc2000/data.html. R factors rendered as labels with levels in metadata; names normalized to kebab-case.") ("time-series" . #f) ("tier" . "bundled") ("package" . "datasets-islr") ("fetch" . #f) ("islr2-chapters" . #hash(("text" . (4)) ("exercises" . (8)))))) ("carseats" . #hash(("name" . "carseats") ("rows" . 400) ("column-count" . 11) ("columns" . (#hash(("name" . "sales") ("original-name" . "Sales") ("type" . "real") ("levels" . ()) ("unit" . "thousands of units") ("description" . "Unit sales (in thousands) at each location") ("missing-count" . 0)) #hash(("name" . "comp-price") ("original-name" . "CompPrice") ("type" . "integer") ("levels" . ()) ("unit" . #f) ("description" . "Price charged by competitor at each location") ("missing-count" . 0)) #hash(("name" . "income") ("original-name" . "Income") ("type" . "integer") ("levels" . ()) ("unit" . #f